+---
+title: "Testing click/utils.py to 100% line+branch coverage"
+author: HarzerHeribert
+date: 2026-10-15
+cost: { minutes: 3, tokens: 41083 }
+touches:
+  - tests/test_utils/test_utils_more.py
+  - src/click/utils.py
+---
+
+## Decided
+- tests/test_utils/test_utils_more.py takes src/click/utils.py to 100% line and branch coverage without touching src/.
+- Platform branches in get_app_dir: monkeypatch `click.utils.WIN` (it is a module global imported from _compat) and `sys.platform`. Do not try to run on the real OS.
+- `_expand_args` imports `from glob import glob` inside the function, so `monkeypatch.setattr("glob.glob", ...)` reaches it. Use that to cover the `re.error` fallback. No real pattern raises re.error on modern Python.
+- `_detect_program_name()` defaults: `monkeypatch.setitem(sys.modules, "__main__", types.ModuleType("__main__"))` plus `sys.argv`. A fresh module has `__package__ = None`, so the basename path is taken.
+
+## Tried and ruled out
+- Looking for a real stream that reaches echo's "bytes but no binary writer" branch (utils.py `if binary_file is not None` false). Only a stream where `write(b"")` fails and there is no `.buffer` reaches it, so echoing bytes to `io.StringIO()` raising TypeError is the realistic case.
+
+## Watch out
+- pytest runs with `filterwarnings = ["error"]`. Close every file a test opens (`_LazyFile`, `open_file(lazy=True)`), or the ResourceWarning fails the run.
+- `addopts = "-m 'not stress'"` is why a run shows ~31000 deselected. Normal tests are not filtered.
+- mypy and pyright only check `src` and `tests/typing`. Editor type errors on duck-typed stubs in `tests/test_utils` are not project errors.
